The microphone differential signals (MIC.MAIN.P and MIC.MAIN.N) \nare very low-level and must be balanced and routed in parallel,\nthe same distance from start to end, same impedance for both signals.\n\nFigure 5 and Figure 6 show typical schematics for microphone input. \nThe microphone filtering capacitor must be as close as possible to the mic. \nThe other components must be as close as possible to the device.\nTPS65920 Layout Guide LineIn LineOut Mic.pdf
